WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:07.660
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.580
The Waimakariri District Council has recently

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.240
reached a lease agreement with Land Information New Zealand

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.300
for much of the Regeneration area land.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.640
This is great news for our community as we can get underway with priority regeneration projects

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.400
while we wait for full land divestment to be completed.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.760
After hearing back from the local community,
Council has approved option two, which will

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.160
see Cass Street closed at the entrance to
the sports and recreation reserve

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.800
and Jollie Street reinstated.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.040
The rebuild of Courtenay Drive has been delayed
by the discovery of asbestos

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.840
in the land underneath the existing road.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.640
Specialists have been appointed to deal with the situation

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.280
and construction of the new road will start in January.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.760
Work has also begun in the Kaiapoi Food Forest.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.400
Fruit trees from red-zoned properties have
been relocated

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.960
and a public planting day recently took place.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.680
We’ll have lot more on this in our next 
 update.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.560
Many of the facilities proposed for the Regeneration
Areas are going to be great for local youth

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.400
and today we’re going find out how they’ve been involved in process so far

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.040
and what they're excited about.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.400
I'm Emma and we're KYDZ, which stands for Kaiapoi Youth Division

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.480
We are all from different schools and we help Kaiapoi be better with our youth.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:29.600
We are excited for the Regeneration for Kaiapoi

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.160
I remember a lot of people, even though we already have McDonald's and fish and chips,

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.920
a lot of people put a lot of takeaways down.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.320
Most kids just hand around at the library these days,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.080
so it would be better to actually have somewhere where we could go.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.280
Maybe around there, there could be some benches, like bleachers.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.840
So, if we have a half-court game and our parents want to come along

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.000
then they can sit on the bleachers and watch us.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.800
Instead of having to use all our petrol and parent's stuff to take us into town,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.720
they could, for once ,come out to us and play us.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.120
Where you can go and pick your own fruit, the trees,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.080
it would be good to have a few more of them around.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.360
I think it will be good, but we need some more stuff to do with shopping

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.800
and other things besides sports.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.440
New spaces to shop and eat was a popular request amongst our youth.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.870
A year ago, Halle Pitama presented ideas from
Tuahiwi School to the Hearing Panel of what

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.440
they wanted in the Recovery Plan.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.860
I talked about things that I'd like to see in the area.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:40.560
Like retail, businesses, more sports fields,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.160
recreation centre - inside and outside.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.720
The whole food forest thing happening over here is great

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.880
because it makes me think about my family's history

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.840
of not just having to go to New World to get food

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.680
that you can come here and I can do something during the weekend, like

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.960
support this whole thing going on and help out, just for the community to

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.580
come back and just something to do.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.480
We also talked to the Waimakariri
Youth Council on progress at their September meeting

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.320
and they were really keen to be involved.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.999
Our next update will be all about the Kaiapoi
Food Forest.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.160
This is a really popular community-led project, and a lot of work has already been done.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.820
And with the roading options confirmed, we’ll look at the updated layout

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.520
for the sports and recreation reserve.

